Bitcoin Lifeboat - Recovery Readiness Audit
===========================================

Status:  Not Ready  (score: 25/100)
Network: testnet
Wallet:  singlesig, wpkh, 1 key(s)

What passed:
  [PASS] Descriptor parsed successfully
  [PASS] Descriptor checksum is valid

Needs attention:
  [WARN] W-NO-CHANGE-DESC  Change descriptor missing
         Export both descriptors from your wallet software. In Sparrow: File > Export Wallet > Output Descriptor. In Bitcoin Core: listdescriptors true.
  [WARN] W-NO-BIRTH-HEIGHT  No wallet birth height documented
         Record the wallet's creation date or the block height at first use alongside your descriptor backup.
  [WARN] W-NO-GAP-LIMIT  Gap limit not documented
         Note the highest address index you have used, or your wallet's configured gap limit, with your backup.
  [WARN] W-NO-KNOWN-ADDRESS  No known address provided
         Re-run the check and paste one address you know belongs to this wallet.
  [WARN] W-NO-PRINTED-BACKUP  No printed descriptor backup
         Print at least two copies of the descriptor backup and store them in separate, secure locations.
  [WARN] W-NO-RECENT-DRILL  No recovery drill in the last 12 months
         Run a Disaster Drill in Lifeboat v0.3 when available, or rehearse a recovery on a test network now.
  [WARN] W-NO-HEIR-INSTRUCTIONS  No heir instructions written
         Write a plain-language recovery runbook for your heirs and store it with your estate documents.
  [WARN] W-NO-EMERGENCY-CONTACT  No emergency contact named
         Name a trusted, Bitcoin-literate contact in your recovery instructions.
  [WARN] W-NO-HW-TEST  Hardware wallet not exercised recently
         Sign a test transaction on a test network with each hardware device.
  [WARN] W-WALLET-SW-UNDOCUMENTED  Wallet software not documented
         Note the wallet software (and version) needed to use this descriptor, and prefer descriptor-based recovery that works in multiple wallets.

What to do next:
  1. Export your change descriptor.  (5 min)
  2. Write down your wallet's creation date or block height.  (5 min)
  3. Document your wallet's gap limit.  (5 min)
  4. Provide one known address from this wallet to compare.  (2 min)
  5. Print two copies of the descriptor backup.  (10 min)
  6. Run a Disaster Drill in Lifeboat v0.3 when available.  (future)
  7. Write recovery instructions for your heirs.  (30 min)
  8. Name a trusted emergency contact.  (5 min)
  9. Sign a test transaction with each hardware device.  (20 min)
  10. Document which wallet software your setup needs.  (5 min)

